+ * near-identical Loop-owner wrapper singletons in pim_core.
+ *
+ * Locking contract: TryLock()-gated on an internal mutex, held for the full
+ * duration of the download (released by Status() on completion, or by
+ * Kill()) -- verified correct, unlike pimServices' confirmed early-release
+ * bug.
+ *
+ * This is the only one of the 7 wrappers with a confirmed SECOND caller
+ * beyond pimEntitlement: pimTestURLDownload() (pim/pim_src/pimTop.cxx), a
+ * standalone diagnostic entry point.
+ *
+ * Confirmed gap (shared with pimShortcuts/pimRegEdit/pimServices):
+ * Cancel() only sets a flag; the owned pimDownloadLoop is not stopped by it.
+ * Unlike those three, however, Status() DOES genuinely populate its
+ * percent/time-remaining output parameters (via pimDownloadLoop::GetStatus()).
+ */
